This lecture demonstrated how **bulk** and **surface micromachining** can be used to fabricate **MEMS-based VOC sensors**. By combining these techniques, it is possible to create sensors with **low power consumption**, **high sensitivity**, and **mechanical stability**. These sensors have wide-ranging applications, from healthcare to industrial safety, and represent a key advancement in MEMS technology.

